    "Question #: 4": {
      "Title": "Exam 400-201 topic 1 question 56 discussion - ExamTopics",
      "Question": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Refer to the exhibit. The Service Provider is deploying Internet service to its VRF customers by using vrf INTERNET. A dedicated firewall provides NAT functionally towards the Internet. Assume that IP address overlapping between VRFs is not an issue."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "image",
            "src": "https://www.examtopics.com/assets/media/exam-media/02728/0004900001.jpg"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Which three configuration steps are required to add Internet service to the VRF customers? (Choose three.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      "Choices": {
        "A": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "A. Export the RD ofvrf INTERNETfrom all customer VRFs."
            }
          ]
        },
        "B": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "B. Import theRD fromvrf INTERNETin all customer VRFs."
            }
          ]
        },
        "C": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "C. C.Leak all VRF routes to the global routing table."
            }
          ]
        },
        "D": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "D. Originate a default route on PE4 invrf INTERNET."
            }
          ]
        },
        "E": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "E. Originate a default route on the firewall invrf INTERNET."
            }
          ]
        },
        "F": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "F. Import the VRF \"INTERNET\" Route Target in all customer VRFs."
            }
          ]
        },
        "G": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "G. Import the Route Target of all customer VRFs invrf INTERNET."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "Answer": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Suggested Answer: BCD \ud83d\uddf3\ufe0f"
          }
        ]
      },
      "Explanation": {
        "content": []
