    "Question #: 18": {
      "Title": "Exam 400-201 topic 2 question 33 discussion - ExamTopics",
      "Question": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "A network engineer is designing the BGP architecture with a requirement of preventing the AS from becoming a Transit AS path, using the following configuration: router bgp 65000 neighbor 10.0.0.1 route-map BGP-ROUTE-POLICY in"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "The goal is to prevent routes learned from 10.0.0.1 from being advertised to any other eBGP peering in the AS 65000. What command should be used within the route map to achieve this goal while keeping existing route policies in place?"
          }
        ]
      },
      "Choices": {
        "A": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "A. set community no-export additive"
            }
          ]
        },
        "B": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "B. set community no-advertise"
            }
          ]
        },
        "C": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "C. set community no-advertise additive"
            }
          ]
        },
        "D": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "D. set community no-export"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "Answer": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Suggested Answer: C \ud83d\uddf3\ufe0f"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Reference: http://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/support/docs/ip/border-gateway-protocol-bgp/26634-bgp-toc.html"
          }
        ]
